<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mart Laar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mart Laar is an Estonian historian and politician who was prime minister from 1992 to 1994 and from 1999 to 2002. His first government carried out radical market reforms, including rapid privatisation, free trade and a flat income tax, which became a model for other post-communist countries.</p></div>
